-- §META_TRANSFORM_REPAIR Terminal (2026-08-16, bim-compiler prompts/4D_GANTT_TM_REFACTOR.md §S10/§S11/§S12)
-- Terminal_meta.db — the pair the live viewer loads through streaming.js §DB_SPLIT_DETECT — carries a
-- per-element-corrupted rebase against Terminal_extracted.db (the extraction truth): 2074 of 48428
-- rows deviate >0.05m from the modal rigid offset (-545.611320, -51.220179, -14.659115), max 11.27m.
-- Corrupted centres flip bearing/containment relations, so the live scheduler classifies a
-- different building from the one every fleet probe measures. geo.db needs no patch: its mesh
-- vertices are local-centred, so a repaired transform carries mesh and bbox with it.
-- Repair threshold is HALF ScheduleGate.EPS (0.025m) so nothing is left within half a tolerance
-- of flipping a predicate. Absolute SET values => idempotent. Generated by
-- scripts/gen_meta_transform_patch.js; detected by scripts/audit_split_pairs.js.
-- FORM: per-row. This meta.db has no elements_rtree, so there is no
-- in-file witness to restore from; values come from Terminal_extracted.db + the modal offset.
